<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African mohair prices mixed at 5th summer sale.</title>
<headline>S.African mohair prices mixed at 5th summer sale.</headline>
<dateline>PORT ELIZABETH, South Africa 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African mohair prices for the fifth summer sale were mixed, the Mohair Board said on Wednesday. There was still very good demand for sale.</p>
<p>Of the 2,837 bales offered 51 percent was sold.</p>
<p>Approximate prices in South African cents a kg:</p>
<p>Adults	  long	 2,300-2,660	(2,300-2,700)</p>
<p>		  medium     1,850-2,360	(1,950-2,302)</p>
<p>		  short	1,850-2,320	(1,702-2,750)</p>
<p>Young Goats   long	 2,450-4,050	(2,450-4,010)</p>
<p>		  medium     2,300-2,800	(2,490-2,702)</p>
<p>		  short	2,400-3,500	(2,492-2,800)</p>
<p>Fine Kids     long	 5,200-13,252     (6,000-11,970)</p>
<p>		  medium     3,500-6,850	(3,850-7,450)</p>
<p>		  short	3,270-4,600	(4,000-4,500)</p>
<p>The sixth sale of the season is scheduled for June 3, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27-11 482 1003</p>
</text>
